  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Write the perpendicular line",
      "body": "<p>The first line is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>, with gradient <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>. The perpendicular line therefore has gradient <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> and passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "Perpendicular nonvertical lines have gradients whose product is -1.",
      "pitfall": "Keep the stated point: the second line does not pass through the first line’s y-intercept.",
      "pause": "Write the equation of the second line.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-extra-straight-lines",
          "reminder": "Perpendicular nonvertical lines have gradients whose product is -1."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Find the triangle’s height",
      "body": "<p>The second line is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>. Equating this to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> finds the intersection, whose y-coordinate is the height above the x-axis.</p>",
      "recap": "A triangle with a base on the x-axis has height equal to the perpendicular vertical distance of its third vertex.",
      "pitfall": "Neither line’s y-intercept is automatically the triangle’s height.",
      "pause": "Solve for the intersection and its y-coordinate.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b2-l02",
          "reminder": "A triangle with a base on the x-axis has height equal to the perpendicular vertical distance of its third vertex."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Use the full base length",
      "body": "<p>Find the base from the two x-intercepts. Use the intersection’s y-coordinate as the perpendicular height, then apply half base times height.</p>",
      "recap": "Triangle area is half base times perpendicular height.",
      "pitfall": "A length is a coordinate difference, not one endpoint coordinate.",
      "pause": "Calculate both dimensions, then use them to find the triangle’s area.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b2-l02",
          "reminder": "Triangle area is half base times perpendicular height."
        }
      ]
    }
